INFO  [Claude Code] ## Summary of Changes
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] I added a new factory method called `createResourceGovernorForReadWriteMethods()` to the test factory class at:
INFO  [Claude Code] `src/test/java/net/finmath/smartcontract/valuation/service/utils/ResourceGovernorDiffblueBase.java`
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### What the Factory Does
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] The new factory method:
INFO  [Claude Code] 1. Creates a `ResourceGovernor` instance with a `PathMatchingResourcePatternResolver`
INFO  [Claude Code] 2. Uses reflection to set the `storageBaseDir` field (which was null and causing the `NullPointerException`)
INFO  [Claude Code] 3. Also sets other required fields (`importDir`, `refinitivConnectionPropertiesFile`, `databaseConnectionPropertiesFile`)
INFO  [Claude Code] 4. Is annotated with `@InterestingTestFactory` so Cover can discover and use it
INFO  [Claude Code] 5. Avoids using mocks (as requested in the issue description)
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### Why This Fixes the Issues
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] Both issues were caused by `Objects.requireNonNull(storageBaseDir)` throwing a `NullPointerException` at:
INFO  [Claude Code] - **Issue 1**: Line 72 in `getReadableResource` method
INFO  [Claude Code] - **Issue 2**: Line 78 in `getWritableResource` method
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] The factory ensures that `storageBaseDir` is initialized with a valid temporary directory path, preventing the NPE.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
